course: dictionary
lesson: 15439
title: Steadfast: loyal and firm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Steadfast means firm and loyal: you stay the same and keep faith with someone, even when it is hard. «Sam was a steadfast friend, even when Ben was in trouble.» Sam did not leave Ben. The clue is that Sam stayed the same.
explain: Steadfast can also mean firm and not moving. «The guard stood steadfast at the gate, even when the wind blew hard.» The guard did not move, so steadfast must mean firm and still. Try your meaning in the sentence: "stood loyal at the gate" feels odd, but "stood firm at the gate" works.
explain: Look for clue words near steadfast, such as friend, love, belief or stood. They often show that it means loyal or firm.
fact: Steadfast means firm and loyal, or firm and not moving.
fact: Steadfast is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a steadfast friend, a steadfast gaze. Its forms are steadfast, more steadfast and most steadfast.
fact: Hans Christian Andersen wrote «The Steadfast Tin Soldier», a story about a toy soldier who stays faithful even when things are very hard.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Rat, Mole and Badger stay steadfast friends to Toad, even when he gets into trouble.
fact: In the Bible, «steadfast love» describes God's faithful love, which never changes.
exercise: «Mum was steadfast in her belief that we would find the lost dog.» What does steadfast mean here? | *Firm, and not giving up | Quick and cheerful | Silly and loud | Tired and sleepy
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to steadfast? | *Loyal | Loud | Lazy | Lost
exercise: Which sentence shows someone who is steadfast? | She forgot her friend's name | He changed his mind every hour | He ran away when his friend needed him | *She stood firm beside her friend, even when it rained all day
test: «The lighthouse keeper kept a steadfast watch through the storm.» What does steadfast suggest? | *Firm, never moving from his post | Quick to run away | Sleepy and bored | Hungry for lunch
test: Which word means the opposite of steadfast? | Firm | Loyal | Faithful | *Changeable
exam: What is the best meaning of steadfast? | Very fast and quick | Full of fear | Sad and lonely | *Firm and loyal, staying the same
